{"kind":"report","text":"Approved source and local validation for exact ccac6b55bd79dc0585d7bf2ef1cfef4fe07899a3 and all 19 artifacts, closing ace84f20 on the scope explicitly recorded by its requester in effective planner assertion 2d5e374b. That assertion transfers every live checker run to 9f81f372 and keeps per-job checker authority open under f12cef6b. This approval claims neither deployed end-to-end proof nor a signed-job/delegation design.\n\nArchitecture: the production checker resolves each immutable job RoomId over the configured ArtroomService ROOM binding before opening its own runner, then submits the signed check to that Room. The service keeps its deep frozen job copy, per-call sessions, measured runner pin, volatility and input bindings. Production src/worker.ts and wrangler.jsonc contain only checker RPC services and runner infrastructure; the harness, publisher, ledger and job-building routes move to src/harness.ts and wrangler.harness.jsonc. Imported and public namespaces are an explicit deployment allowlist. These changes fit the current Room job shape; packages/room is byte-identical to approved main, not a disguised merge of A's still-unapproved dispatch changes. A's cleanup and dispatch correctness remains under review 013dad0c and its successor.\n\nSecurity: the code conforms to the existing R-EXEC-8 operator trust boundary, which explicitly trusts bound Room producers and leaves jobs unsigned. A bound caller can cause work before Room admission; a service binding is not proof that an individual job was recorded. The signing key acts as a room member, with actual Room membership, role and revocation deciding admission. Runner/key/credential separation, exact checkout and snapshot isolation remain in force; runner pin mismatch destroys its new modeled container and signs/runs nothing, and the volatile reviewer refuses volatile:false before opening a runner. The new Room resolver tests use a fake resolver/ledger, so their unknown-room and membership behavior is not deployed proof. The follow-up authority decision and its threat model remain open under f12cef6b, and 9f81 must prove the actual deployed Room-dispatched check/review/land flow.\n\nSimplification: one deployment now serves multiple Rooms through one resolver; fixed-Room expectations remain only for the harness/tests, and per-room ROOM_ID/CHECKER_DELEGATION settings leave production. A single parsed namespace allowlist and a physically separate harness configuration make the deployment boundary clear. The LLM reviewer fetches job.base by ID rather than inferring the first parent; if the base is unreadable it reviews only the available tree and says so. The shipped reviewer configuration is advisory and volatile; tests/types configurations are valid and match their checkers. No functional scope was removed because of estimates.\n\nValidation: fresh npm ci (374 packages), root npm run typecheck exit 0, all 45 checker tests passed, production and harness deployment dry-runs both exit 0 (40.13/127.78 KiB local bundles). Three own actual checker/local Git component controls also passed: filtered unavailable base excludes private content and reports whole available-tree review; whole-tree unavailable base explicitly reports fallback; base==integration yields an empty change and avoids an extra base fetch. Diagnostics are retained at /tmp/artroom-checker-G-Am3-v1-diagnostics and removed from the clean candidate checkout. There was no checker deployment, new credential creation or live inference. No fresh full-root or Git Workers test claim: other packages are byte-identical to main fecd69eb, whose approved gates f542a933/7f532549/f566d5ad and prior reviews are credited; builder separately reports exact-head root and Git Workers gates exit 0.\n\nPrimary report read first, all 19 changed paths fully read in source or complete diffs, including all 354 moved harness lines and full production Worker. Remaining 561 tree entries match approved main. The merge 27563fc6 preserves all disjoint parent changes, introduces no novel merge blob and deletes no main file. The earlier G5 snapshot identity/per-snapshot repository/known-ID isolation and durable cleanup fixes are preserved and re-exercised by the candidate suite. Scope and local assessment are also recorded in checker assertion d74cdc5e. Approval is for the complete source delivery under the recorded scope transfer; 9f81 live integration, f12cef6b authority, full Pi/MCP contracts, Room layout-2 adoption and wake/schedule work remain separately open.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ede682ce8e6d4b8ac06e035802fb079d2806397d","binding":"assigned","head":"ccac6b55bd79dc0585d7bf2ef1cfef4fe07899a3","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a09f0390a0b8ab48ad4c17a974228f1e3123d28b\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d74cdc5e1c6504cc2240cf78ca949cdc95255089\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:cb923a2661704e179a8ab02bf519eaaff4812e09\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2d5e374b6975cedaac2b29c1dc587cbff79ba0a3","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}